47671" :question/id #uuid "6364a192-b48f-5703-8297-b5247d60439d" :question/math-academy-id "q-147671" :question/problem "Consider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nA triangle $S$ has vertices at $(-1,-1),(0,2),$ and $(-2,1).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the action of $T?$\n\n- $(6,-1)$\n- $(7,-14)$\n- $(8,-16)$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of $S$ under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -3 \\\\ 10 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & -6 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 12 & -14\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(8,-16),$ $(-6,12)$, and $(7,-14).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-147671/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-147671"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-21066/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "5793788d-3e8a-5de4-8fa8-3a204a33d393" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21066/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "3a33fb9b-b0fb-50ac-8e4a-fe3b9900b72c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21066/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a