matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}12 & 4 & 12 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(12,6)$, $(4,2)$ and $(12,6).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-21066/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca93cd65-65e3-521e-a1e3-2721f45fb6a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-21066"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-21061"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/5c0196b13b3f20ba05313a9604e73b13251937b525a12fd5b9997e99f4ae21a0.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(-1,1)$, $(1,-1),$ $(-1,1).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/2f8d6ec6c9a71e61180ad04c25d623c40dadfdd623e1e2eaa8458915bcaca2f8.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-21063/selection/64d2c1c9dd2ea990f48b9a36ed1ffea97fa3d2dbcd0460ccb294835db7bf20e9" :answer/id #uuid "0f4b8ff3-6f9e-5e75-9a7e-86d7a7b55fde" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/b4d2150d92ff14a654fb7079a17d7bd75abe721c0d37d4075d5a92635bafc170.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21063/selection/3a80f23d605e2eb0c4d2377c4d0988509f7a6735d58b7851f3655026f55dad1e" :answer/id #uuid "34880a8f-4354-522a-8d0d-3ed1d347e87c" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/ee4a96b2b1106fbd1a5ec222c3f7f2a5e5a9e84c9bfe539aeb29a1918943aef9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21063/selection/2413ed823237bc899994d80619d35f7e967c6f233d0f89b5bf8fcd16f638b498" :answer/id #uuid "ec7cdc35-c43f-5b8a-adf1-45e56f6e2a2e" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/92beb71e7d09cba01f2eeb82a60ca3b0b3929064e4f16da3af104db8c5eaa8df.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21063/selection/16832473d65f511daa3fc10e3bf909fa4c21ab552b1d05ebe7aacc079fd5e67a" :answer/id #uuid "9db75bfc-fe19-51e4-ab27-cf8792f76f05" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/40f352980b38be63b071b160953eff23a98996dce58c5f616e10958a8a70182e.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-21063/selection/140e06846e20705e62f7c743c2dba88d3d5719273bb5809da46aec895748f6e4