ademy-id "q-21058" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/fee79ec0b214a4ba87400b4b8c9dab2c623878d067821c572b26ae241625c48a.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 & 5 \\\\ 10 & 15 & 25\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(2,10)$, $(3,15)$, and  $(5,25).$  Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/bf5987fde11416780a6a599e3952db7319e1c0e859e2439b7df70c5659bc6839.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-21058/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d1252e9-f2ac-5adf-9cf5-ef48e35fb747"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-21058"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97024/selection/1e4ceecf23a674a5619d0fb4a5522398159993f896b21d541bfd280408aaa641" :answer/id #uuid "0a76143f-0c8c-5249-b635-c90a0d991c18" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13993138/assets/a209f0e3b428ba48d6cc2d21c50706820ff4524c13c8b012aea4d5d2dc4e60b1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-970